In Angular, a shared component is a component that can be used across multiple modules in your application. Here are the steps to create a shared component:

1. Create a new directory in your Angular project to hold your shared components. For example, create a directory called `shared` in the root of your project.

2. Create a new Angular component in the `shared` directory. You can use the Angular CLI to create a new component by running the following command in your terminal:
```
ng generate component shared/my-shared-component
```
This will create a new directory called `my-shared-component` in your `shared` directory, containing the component's HTML, CSS, and TypeScript files.

3. In your component's TypeScript file (`my-shared-component.component.ts`), add the `@Component` decorator to define your component. For example:
```
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-shared-component',
  templateUrl: './my-shared-component.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./my-shared-component.component.css']
})
export class MySharedComponent {
  @Input() title: string;
}
```
In this example, the component has a `title` input property that can be set by the component's parent.

4. Create a template for your component in its HTML file (`my-shared-component.component.html`). For example:
```
<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
```
This template displays the component's `title` property.

5. To make your component available across multiple modules, you need to declare it in the `declarations` array of your module's `NgModule` decorator. You can do this by creating a separate file for your component's exports, for example `shared.module.ts`:
```
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { MySharedComponent } from './my-shared-component.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [MySharedComponent],
  exports: [MySharedComponent],
  imports: [CommonModule]
})
export class SharedModule { }
```
6. Finally, import your `SharedModule` in the modules that want to use your shared component. For example, in your `app.module.ts`:
```
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { AppComponent } from './app.component';
import { MySharedComponent } from './shared/my-shared-component.component';
import { SharedModule } from './shared/shared.module';

